## Following the Data in the Lab Code

<div style="line-height: 2;">
  <div style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.25;">Your students' classifier lab uses names they did not write: three imports from <code style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1; padding: 0 4px;">helpers</code>, a trained model, and a dictionary for today's features. Step through a similar program, one line at a time, to see what each name holds. The lab also uses temperature and traffic as features, instead of the snowfall and visibility you just saw.</div>
</div>

